    "Scouting Notes": "Average defender at third base who handled the position well enough to fill in at shortstop at times in college.\n Senior year he tapped into previously unrealized power.\n Above average bat speed, but his power is average.\n Takes big swings, but over his Louisville career he showed pretty good bat to ball skills and he knows how to take a walk.\n Solid defender with an above average arm.\n Pro debut went well and got an aggressive move up to High A early on.\n Some K issues to start, but showing some power as he's gone deep 3 times, including twice to straight away center.",
